#
# Counter-example for math:ProbabilitySpaceCompleteShape (Rule P4): a math:ProbabilitySpace
# that names its sample space Ω (math:sampleSpace) and its event σ-algebra ℱ
# (math:eventSigmaAlgebra) but OMITS its probability measure P (math:probabilityMeasure),
# so the third component's sh:minCount 1 fires — shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent
# (math:IncompleteProbabilitySpace).
# Single violation: the other two Kolmogorov-triple components are present as IRIs so their
# minCount/nodeKind arms stay SATISFIED; no math:ProbabilityMeasure node is present so
# math:ProbabilityMeasureShape / math:MeasureCompletenessShape do not fire — EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilitySpace / math:IncompleteProbabilitySpace (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilitySpaceIncompleteBad).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:incompleteSpace a math:ProbabilitySpace ;
    math:sampleSpace ex:omega ;
    math:eventSigmaAlgebra ex:borelAlgebra .

ex:omega a math:SymbolicSampleSpace .
ex:borelAlgebra a math:BorelSigmaAlgebra .
